---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const B = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<Base title="ΒΛΑΞ — in English" palette="charti"
  description="A reluctant English summary of ΒΛΑΞ: a DJ duo and party series from Grevena, Greece. The dialect stays untranslated.">
  <article class="reading" lang="en">
    <h1>In English, reluctantly</h1>
    <p>
      ΒΛΑΞ (roughly: "dolt"; the word is indeclinable here by decree, in both our languages) is a
      DJ duo and a party series — four parties, 2016–2019, every year around Christmas — at Fuit
      Art Cafe, Ηλία Φάσσα 2, Grevena, Greece (2012–2023; the owner now runs Sun Do Each in
      Thessaloniki — the best sandwiches in town, per the duo, who are objective). Two brothers-in-law-in-aspiration (μπατζανάκια:
      men married to sisters — except they never found the sisters), one of whom is the idiot and
      one the broke one. We do not say which is which. A proof assistant was consulted; it did
      not terminate.
    </p>
    <p>
      The parties featured Greek 80s-adjacent kitsch played with love and scholarship, teddy
      bears (dismembered, cherished), lollipops at 2€ per hundred that dye your tongue purple for
      about a year, a PAOK chant in three renditions, and a dance technique called σκρολτς whose
      all-time record (411, Düsseldorf, sprained knee) this website's scroll counter respects.
    </p>
    <p>
      Everything else on this site — the short story, the timeline with its honest red asterisks,
      the disputes page, the booking terms — is in Greek, because that is the language it
      happened in. The dialect of Grevena stays untransliterated everywhere. If you have reached
      this page by accident: <a href={`${B}/`}>προς ΒΛΑΞ</a>. If on purpose: ask a Greek friend,
      preferably one who has been to a bar in the Balkans after 3am.
    </p>
    <p class="small muted">
      Bookings: we do very selective djings. Ask for a quote and we will see if we can do it.
      No discounts; work is work.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
<style>
  h1 { color: var(--fg); }
</style>
